<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Wimpfen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1622</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Wimpfen was fought on 6 May 1622 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bad-wimpfen">Bad Wimpfen</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neckar">Neckar</a>, when the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholic-league">Catholic League</a> under Tilly, with Spanish troops under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gonzalo-fernandez-de-cordoba">Gonzalo Fernández de Córdoba</a>, defeated Margrave George Frederick of Baden-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durlach">Durlach</a>. It was part of the campaign in which the Catholic powers conquered the Electoral Palatinate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-wimpfen.jpg" alt="Battle of Wimpfen" width="320" height="178" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sebastiaen Vrancx · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sebastiaan_Vrancx_-_Battle_of_Vimpfen_on_6_May_1622.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
